WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.635
-Good evening.
I'm Seth Meyers.

00:00:02.701 --> 00:00:04.303
This is "Late Night."
We hope you're doing well.

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:05.804
And now, if you don't mind,
I'm going to get to the news.

00:00:05.871 --> 00:00:08.507
A Manhattan jury on Friday
ordered former President Trump

00:00:08.574 --> 00:00:12.078
to pay nearly $84 million
in his civil defamation case.

00:00:12.145 --> 00:00:17.717 line:0%
Well, that explains
the new fundraising amounts.

00:00:17.784 --> 00:00:20.753
Former President Trump said
at a rally in Las Vegas

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:23.422
over the weekend that he feels,
quote, "Sharper now

00:00:23.489 --> 00:00:24.757
than I did 20 years ago."

00:00:24.824 --> 00:00:27.093
Of course, based on
all of his testimony,

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:32.064
he doesn't remember a single
thing from 20 years ago.

00:00:32.131 --> 00:00:34.733
The White House is set to hold
a live streamed event tomorrow

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:35.969
with high school students.

00:00:36.035 --> 00:00:38.838
The event is called
Seniors for Seniors.

00:00:42.308 --> 00:00:45.345
The Biden campaign is reportedly
hoping to get an endorsement

00:00:45.412 --> 00:00:47.514
from Taylor Swift,
though personally,

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:50.150
I think they're going
about it all wrong.

00:00:52.685 --> 00:00:54.554
When asked in an interview
yesterday

00:00:54.621 --> 00:00:57.289
about former President Trump's
false birther attacks

00:00:57.356 --> 00:00:58.691
against her,
presidential candidate

00:00:58.758 --> 00:01:01.327
Nikki Haley said, quote,
"When he feels threatened,

00:01:01.394 --> 00:01:03.496
he starts to throw all kinds
of things out there."

00:01:03.563 --> 00:01:04.497
Said Trump,

00:01:04.564 --> 00:01:06.466
"She's sleeping with Fauci."

00:01:09.202 --> 00:01:11.804
California Governor Gavin Newsom
said in an interview yesterday

00:01:11.871 --> 00:01:13.606
that Democrats have done
a much better job

00:01:13.673 --> 00:01:16.175
in recent months of
selling their accomplishments,

00:01:16.242 --> 00:01:18.411
and added that the party
has the receipts

00:01:18.477 --> 00:01:20.313
from three years
of the Biden administration.

00:01:20.379 --> 00:01:22.047
Because,
like most guys his age,

00:01:22.114 --> 00:01:25.952
Biden's been keeping
all of them in his wallet.

00:01:26.019 --> 00:01:29.489
"Yeah, you never know.
You never know

00:01:29.556 --> 00:01:30.756
when you're going
to need a receipt

00:01:30.823 --> 00:01:33.492
to prove you bought something.

00:01:33.559 --> 00:01:36.695
Just -- Just keep it with you.

00:01:36.762 --> 00:01:38.064
Keep it in your wallet."

00:01:38.131 --> 00:01:40.967
In a new interview,
Republican Senator Tim Scott

00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:42.535
said that average Americans
are, quote,

00:01:42.602 --> 00:01:45.704
"Not talking about the lawsuits
against former President Trump."

00:01:45.771 --> 00:01:47.240
You know what else
they're not talking about?

00:01:47.306 --> 00:01:50.777
[Whispers] Tim Scott.

00:01:50.844 --> 00:01:54.080
Russian President Vladimir Putin
was formally registered today

00:01:54.147 --> 00:01:55.548
for the upcoming election
in March.

00:01:55.615 --> 00:01:58.651
And I've seen enough --
with zero precincts reporting,

00:01:58.718 --> 00:02:00.787
I'm calling it for Putin.

00:02:04.123 --> 00:02:07.626
A man in -- [ Laughs ]
A man in California

00:02:07.693 --> 00:02:09.229
recently set
the Guinness World Record

00:02:09.295 --> 00:02:11.531
for largest collection
of hotel keycards,

00:02:11.598 --> 00:02:13.399
and in a very related story,

00:02:13.465 --> 00:02:16.536
they finally caught
the Sacramento Strangler.

00:02:20.139 --> 00:02:21.774
I felt the same way
when I read it.

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:26.446
It makes you laugh at first,
and then you're like, "Oh, God."

00:02:26.512 --> 00:02:28.214
Climate activists
at the Louvre in Paris

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:30.649
over the weekend threw
pumpkin soup on the Mona Lisa,

00:02:30.716 --> 00:02:32.685
though I think it's
a little off message

00:02:32.752 --> 00:02:36.256
to go after a lady
who didn't even have a car.

00:02:40.893 --> 00:02:43.463
Oh. Is that --
Was that the issue?

00:02:43.529 --> 00:02:45.832
Oh, what was --
That joke was cut?

00:02:45.898 --> 00:02:47.834
Oh, interesting. Yeah.

00:02:50.002 --> 00:02:53.339
Well, I -- Well, I can't say
we were proven wrong.

00:02:56.141 --> 00:02:58.710
So I'm sorry -- So there's
a lot wrong with it,

00:02:58.777 --> 00:03:02.649
but was the issue that the ring
thing was up the whole time?

00:03:02.715 --> 00:03:04.717
That was one of the issues?
Yeah, yeah.

00:03:08.788 --> 00:03:10.523
Certainly going to be
an interesting meeting

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:13.759
after the show.

00:03:13.826 --> 00:03:15.627
I hope at least there's one
person there who's like,

00:03:15.694 --> 00:03:17.297
"I thought it went good."

00:03:19.798 --> 00:03:22.468
The doorbell security camera
company Ring --

00:03:22.535 --> 00:03:23.703
Do we want to go
to the next graphic,

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:25.371
or do we want to keep this?

00:03:27.873 --> 00:03:31.377
The doorbell security camera
company Ring announced last week

00:03:31.443 --> 00:03:33.379
that it would no longer
allow police departments

00:03:33.446 --> 00:03:36.916
to request users' footage,
but then reminded customers

00:03:36.983 --> 00:03:39.151
that they do still have
a binding contract

00:03:39.218 --> 00:03:43.288
with "America's
Funniest Home Videos."

00:03:43.355 --> 00:03:47.026
A French tourist at Arkansas's
Crater of Diamonds State Park

00:03:47.093 --> 00:03:48.794
recently found
a seven carat diamond.

00:03:48.861 --> 00:03:50.129
Wow, that is hard to believe --

00:03:50.195 --> 00:03:53.666
someone in France
took a vacation to Arkansas?

00:03:56.869 --> 00:03:58.804
The locals must have been
super psyched

00:03:58.871 --> 00:04:01.240
when<i> they</i> found the diamond.

00:04:01.307 --> 00:04:04.877
[French accent]
"Oh, look at this."

00:04:07.746 --> 00:04:14.120
[ Speaking gibberish ]

00:04:14.187 --> 00:04:16.155
[ Sighs ] Just a lot --
A lot's happened

00:04:16.222 --> 00:04:18.424
this monologue.
I just feel like --

00:04:18.491 --> 00:04:19.692
I mean, it's almost over,

00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:21.461
but I feel like
we've been through a lot.

00:04:23.763 --> 00:04:26.999
And finally, a Russian man who
flew from Denmark to Los Angeles

00:04:27.066 --> 00:04:28.334
without a passport last year

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:30.770
was found guilty last week
of being a stowaway

00:04:30.836 --> 00:04:33.672
and faces up to five years
in prison or worse,

00:04:33.739 --> 00:04:35.508
a return flight
on Alaska Airlines.

00:04:35.574 --> 00:04:37.176
You guys!

00:04:37.243 --> 00:04:39.044
I feel like
a couple more weeks --

00:04:39.111 --> 00:04:41.046
a couple more weeks where
that'll be a fair punchline.

00:04:41.113 --> 00:04:43.983
You guys, that was a monologue.
We made it. We made it through.

